{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>ונהי</b> Twice in the Masorah: here, ונהי בעינינו כחגבים; and ונהי כטמא כלנו. וכן היינו בעיניהם in gematria is קן נמלים, and thus also כ\"ן גם כן is notarikon: וכמו נמלים. With this one can settle what Rashi explained, \"we heard them say: נמלים בכרם\" — for whoever mentions the name of ants, but does the verse not say ונהי בעינינו כחגבים וכן היינו בעיניהם, which implies כחגבים and not כנמלים? Rather, as we have said, it appears that Rashi is being precise, end of quote. ונהי כטמא כולנו — because at that time the decree סורו טמא was decreed upon them, or as written ככה יאכלו לחמם טמא:" "<b>כחגבים</b> Twice in the Masorah. Here, and the other: ויושביה כחגבים, as found in the Midrash — that one grasshopper ate a pomegranate and cast away the peel, and all twelve spies entered to sit inside it for shade. And this is ויושביה כחגבים — they sat in it like grasshoppers:"], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "The gematria and notarikon chain is transmitted as found: וכן היינו בעיניהם = קן נמלים; כ\"ן גם כן expands to וכמו נמלים. The quotation from Rashi ends at ע\"כ."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:22:12.210455054Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}